  "body": "### Summary\nCapture how HFR answers the id form of a topic link and a stale slug, logged out and logged in, so that the About links to the app's own topics (LOT-120 (#211)) can use stable id-based URLs and open in the app without guessing.\n\nScope\n- GET, read-only, page 1 only, logged out then logged in: `/forum2.php?config=hfr.inc&cat=25&post=1711&page=1` ([TU] Super HFR+) and `/forum2.php?config=hfr.inc&cat=25&subcat=528&post=8811&page=1` (beta topic). Record status, `Location` chain and final URL (HFR-PROTOCOL R5 has the logged-in 301 for topic 1711 page 450 only).\n- GET a stale slug of the same topic (an older title slug, e.g. the one in legacy `Classes/HFRDebugViewController.m:23`): redirect, 404 or page?\n- Both topics are in the Apple category hidden for App Review (Q-7): record whether the logged-out answer differs.\n- Anonymize, add MANIFEST rows and settle the matching rows in HFR-PROTOCOL (R5, §7).\n\nSources: legacy `Classes/OfflineMessagesTableViewController.m:78` (id form), `SuperHFRplus/Assets/HTML/credits.html:12` (slug link); community study of the HFR+ topics (2026-10-28).\n\nWanted by: LOT-120 (#211), LOT-095 (#187).\n\nAcceptance criteria\n- Captures of both id forms (logged out and in) and of one stale slug, anonymized, in `captures/` with MANIFEST rows.\n- `check --corpus` is clean.\n",
